Research on Human Curiosity Modelling in RL environment 05/2024-09/2025
Participated in designing a system containing a basic forecasting module and a curiosity reward module...
Use density and prediction error as curiosity measure and applied Mutual Information to compute good representations of state-action pair based on the Information Bottleneck theory;
Design of a Four-legged Robot Dog 02/2023-07/2024
Designed a four-legged robot dog and participated in a robot obstacle XXX and robot race in the ROBOCON China University Robot Competition;

Design of a XXX-legged Jumping Delta Robot 08/2023-03/2024
Responsible for debugging the QP algorithm and troubleshooting hardware communication issues.
Designed a XXX-legged delta robot that could jump in the direction and at the speed as instructed;
Simulated robots using MuJoCo and trained robots using the PPO algorithm;
Designed a reward function to encourage robots to jump as close as possible to the given speed and tilt as little as possible.

INTERNSHIPS
Galaxea AI Technology Co., Ltd. 06/2024-08/2024
Built simulation and training environment;
Designed reward function, constructed neural networks, and configured update policies;
Enabled the robotic arm to open the door successfully using A2C and TRPO algorithms.

Institute of Automation Chinese Academy of Sciences 06/2023-08/2023
Enabled grasping and obstacle avoidance of both a single robotic arm and a humanoid robot by building simulation models using NVIDIA's cuRobo platform;
Applied AnyGrasp to generate accurate grasp poses efficiently and employed IK enumeration to map out reachable poses for trajectory planning;
XXX the robot's reachable space by about 20% to 50% by coordinating the robot's waist rotation and arm movement;
Human-computer interaction: which could perform actions according to instructions and XXX for help while in trouble;
Integrated MGDT algorithm into MindSpore architecture to enable parallel computing with multiple graphics cards in XXX computer;
Built a simulation environment of a robot picking up things from a refrigerator using Isaac Gym to collect data for model training.
